<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8116" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circŭlātor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A pedler</i>: auctionum, Asin. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				10, 32, 3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A mountebank</i>, <i>quack</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 5,
				27, 3</span></i>; Petr 68, 6; <i><span class="en">Dig. 47,
				11, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Ben. 6, 11, 2</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">App. M. 1, p. 103,
			38</span></i>.—Of noisy philosophers, <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep.
				29, 5</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
